# TeleD - Advanced Telegram Saved Messages Downloader

[![Python Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.9%2B-blue.svg)](https://python.org)
[![TUI Framework](https://img.shields.io/badge/framework-Textual%200.50%2B-green.svg)](https://textual.textualize.io/)
[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-purple.svg)](LICENSE)

**TeleD** is a high-performance, asynchronous terminal user interface (TUI) for indexing, searching, and downloading media files from Telegram **Saved Messages** (`me`).

Designed with a modern terminal aesthetic inspired by **LazyGit**, **Lazydocker**, and **btop**, TeleD combines real-time search, non-blocking asynchronous file streaming, automated error recovery, and SQLite WAL query optimization.

---

## 🌟 Key Features

- **Saved Messages Browser**: Scans and caches downloadable media (Videos, PDFs, ZIP/RAR, Images, Audio, Documents).
- **Lazy Loading & Virtual Table Pagination**: Supports **100,000+ files** seamlessly with instant (<5ms) windowed pagination rendering (`250 items/page`).
- **Instant Search Engine**: Real-time fuzzy searching powered by **RapidFuzz** across filenames, extensions (`*.mkv`, `*.pdf`, `*.zip`, `*.iso`), MIME types, and upload dates.
- **SQLite WAL Query Engine**: 100% database-level sorting (`ORDER BY`) and category filtering (`WHERE`) using compound indexes (`idx_files_ext_date`, `idx_files_dl_date`, `idx_files_fn_date`). Zero Python memory sorting.
- **Robust Downloader Engine**:
  - Resumes partial downloads automatically with 4KB chunk boundary alignment.
  - Multi-item download queue supporting sequential and configurable concurrent downloads (1–10).
  - Exponential backoff retry mechanism (max 5 retries).
  - Automatic **FloodWait** handling (sleeps exact duration + 1s without burning retry quota).
  - Post-download size & integrity verification to prevent file corruption.
- **Comprehensive Error Handling**:
  - Automatic SQLite database corruption detection & auto-repair (`tele_metadata.db.corrupted.<timestamp>`).
  - Intercepts Disk Full (`errno 28`), Permission Denied, Network Drops, and Session Revocation cleanly.
- **Modern UI & Aesthetic**:
  - Btop-inspired dual-pane interface with dark/light themes.
  - Colored file type badges (`[PDF]`, `[VIDEO]`, `[ZIP]`, `[IMG]`, `[AUDIO]`, `[DOC]`).
  - Live progress rows with EWMA speed calculation, ETA, and total queue metrics.
  - Full mouse support (scrolling, header sorting, row selection).

---

## 🏗 Architecture & Design Principles

TeleD follows strict **SOLID** principles, Clean Architecture, and Dependency Injection:

```
                  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
                  │          Textual App UI             │
                  │   MainScreen / Settings / Modals    │
                  └──────────────────┬──────────────────┘
                                     │
                  ┌──────────────────▼──────────────────┐
                  │      Dependency Injection (DI)      │
                  │          ServiceContainer           │
                  └─────────┬─────────────────┬─────────┘
                            │                 │
           ┌────────────────▼──┐           ┌──▼──────────────────┐
           │      Browser      │           │     Downloader      │
           │ Message Browser   │           │ Async Queue Engine  │
           └────────┬──────────┘           └──┬──────────────────┘
                    │                         │
           ┌────────▼──────────┐           ┌──▼──────────────────┐
           │  TelegramClient   │           │    SQLite Database  │
           │  Telethon Wrapper │           │ WAL Schema & Index  │
           └───────────────────┘           └─────────────────────┘
```

- **Single Responsibility Principle (SRP)**: UI components, Database I/O, Telegram API, and Download Engine are completely decoupled.
- **Dependency Injection**: Services are registered and managed via `ServiceContainer` (`tgdl/services/container.py`).
- **File Size Compliance**: Every Python module in `tgdl/` strictly adheres to a maximum size of **300 lines**.

---

## 📦 Installation & Setup

### Prerequisites
- Python **3.9+**
- Active Telegram Account

### 1. Developer / Editable Installation
Clone the repository and install TeleD in editable mode:
```bash
git clone https://github.com/truvx/TeleD.git
cd TeleD
pip install -e .
```
This registers the global CLI executable `teled`.

### 2. Standalone Binary Installer (PyInstaller)
To package TeleD as a single-file standalone executable for distribution:
```bash
pip install pyinstaller
pyinstaller --onefile --name teled tgdl/app.py
```
The generated binary will be placed in `dist/teled`.

---

## 🚀 Usage Guide

### First-Time Launch & Configuration
Run TeleD from any terminal:
```bash
teled
```
If configuration `.env` is missing, TeleD will guide you through interactive setup:
1. Obtain your `API_ID` and `API_HASH` from [my.telegram.org](https://my.telegram.org/).
2. TeleD automatically saves credentials into `.env` and reuses your authorized session in `tgdl/session/` across restarts.

---

## ⌨ Keyboard Shortcuts Matrix

| Keybinding | Action Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `Ctrl+P`, `Ctrl+F`, `F` | Focus Search Bar |
| `Esc` | Clear Search Filter & Return Focus to Data Table |
| `Space` | Toggle Selection on Highlighted Row |
| `Ctrl+A` | Select All Items on Current Page |
| `Ctrl+D` | Clear Selection |
| `Enter` | Queue Selected Files for Download |
| `C` | Cycle Category Filter (`Videos`, `Images`, `PDF`, `Documents`, `Archives`, `Audio`, `All`) |
| `]` / `Right` | Next Page |
| `[` / `Left` | Previous Page |
| `Ctrl+R`, `R` | Sync / Refresh Saved Messages from Telegram |
| `Ctrl+L` | Focus Active Download Queue Pane |
| `Ctrl+S`, `S` | Open Settings Modal Screen |
| `P` | Pause / Resume Queue Engine |
| `X` | Cancel All Pending Downloads in Queue |
| `Alt+R` | Retry Failed Downloads |
| `T` | Toggle Dark / Light Visual Theme |
| `Q` | Quit Application |

---

## 🔧 Diagnostics & Logging

Structured logs are automatically written to `logs/teled.log`.

To adjust logging verbosity via environment variables:
```bash
TELED_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG teled
```

